# Marjin — Vercel deployment boundary (ALLOWLIST). Review: artifacts/p0-vercel-surface-hardening/
#
# Vercel project preset "Other", no build step, no `public/` directory: every uploaded file
# outside api/, node_modules/ and the package/lock files becomes a STATIC file of the
# deployment, and static files take precedence over the catch-all rewrite. So "uploaded"
# means "publicly downloadable". Only runtime inputs are uploaded; everything else at the
# project root is excluded. A new top-level file or directory is excluded by default and
# must be classified in test/support/vercel-surface.mjs before it can be allowed here.
#
# Guarded by test/security/vercel-deployment-surface.test.mjs.

# 1. Exclude everything at the project root …
/*

# 2. … then re-allow the runtime inputs.
# Browser runtime (served statically; `/` → landing.html, `/app` → index.html)
!/index.html
!/landing.html
# Financial Core browser bundle (slice C1 loads /fincore/v1/**; absent until B1)
!/fincore
# Serverless functions and the modules they import (traced by @vercel/nft)
!/api
!/src
!/lib
# Deployment and build inputs
!/vercel.json
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/tsconfig.json

# 3. Never upload these, even inside an allowed directory.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.crt
**/*service-account*.json
**/*serviceAccount*.json
**/*credentials*.json
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
**/*~
**/*.test.*
